WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.344
This chapter asks a specific question: A living technical book needs

2
00:00:04.344 --> 00:00:08.627
a versioned claim lifecycle that separates what an assertion says from

3
00:00:08.627 --> 00:00:12.911
what evidence currently supports it and preserves why each state change

4
00:00:12.911 --> 00:00:13.690
was accepted.

5
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.822
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: Citations, passing validators, proof objects,

6
00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:24.093
benchmark scores, and polished prose do not by themselves identify the

7
00:00:24.093 --> 00:00:29.364
exact claim atom, evidence role, scope, independence, causal link, negative result,

8
00:00:29.364 --> 00:00:31.760
or accepted transition they justify.

9
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.292
The chapter's core claim is this: Each material claim should have

10
00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:42.225
a stable identity, versioned text and scope, claim label, support state,

11
00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:44.915
non-aggregating evidence-quality vector, and transition ledger;

12
00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:50.392
upward movement is allowed only through an accepted claim-specific transition whose

13
00:00:50.392 --> 00:00:55.530
artifacts and evidence roles meet declared gates, while contradiction, failed verification,

14
00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:00.667
missing support, and scope mismatch remain eligible to narrow, downgrade, refute,

15
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.535
or deprecate the claim.

16
00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:07.852
Project canonical claim records and accepted transition lineage into Appendix C

17
00:01:07.852 --> 00:01:12.830
as the public claim ledger without treating that projection as evidence.

18
00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.460
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

19
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.162
A canonical claim record, evidence transition record, non-aggregating evidence cell,

20
00:01:23.162 --> 00:01:27.987
public Appendix C projection, one bounded six-project lineage cell,

21
00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:33.885
and executable positive and rejecting suites for missing bindings, absent evidence,

22
00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:36.030
negative-result deletion, dimension aggregation,

23
00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:42.372
scope strengthening, lineage splicing, false independence, stale projections, and support-state laundering,

24
00:01:42.372 --> 00:01:45.100
with no chapter-core support movement.

25
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:50.588
Represent claim label, support state, lifecycle state, and terminal disposition as

26
00:01:50.588 --> 00:01:54.801
distinct fields so assertion kind, current backing, review status,

27
00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:58.545
and outcome cannot collapse into one confidence word.

28
00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:04.558
Permit source-derived movement only from a passage-reviewed, exact claim mapping that

29
00:02:04.558 --> 00:02:09.715
records the source's evidence role, interpretation boundary, contradictions, and non-claims.

30
00:02:10.315 --> 00:02:14.694
The design can still fail. Support-state inflation. Citation laundering.

31
00:02:14.694 --> 00:02:20.046
Silent removal of failed claims. Ownership laundering. The correct response is

32
00:02:20.046 --> 00:02:25.399
to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate, or retain an owned residual rather

33
00:02:25.399 --> 00:02:27.345
than narrate uncertainty away.

34
00:02:27.945 --> 00:02:32.991
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

35
00:02:32.991 --> 00:02:37.120
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

36
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:42.166
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

37
00:02:42.166 --> 00:02:42.625
closed.

38
00:02:42.965 --> 00:02:47.932
A reachable lifecycle freezes exact atom and proposition/obligation/predicate projections,

39
00:02:47.932 --> 00:02:52.899
derives non-aggregating target evidence, preserves negative evidence and non-claims,

40
00:02:52.899 --> 00:02:58.970
and cannot assign support, move related claims, or create external effects.

41
00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:03.465
A claim cannot be promoted when required evidence is absent.

42
00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:09.029
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

43
00:03:09.029 --> 00:03:13.993
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

44
00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:18.957
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

45
00:03:18.957 --> 00:03:23.470
enforcement. No safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI, or ASI conclusion follows.

46
00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:28.285
These boundaries matter because an explanatory derivative is useful only if

47
00:03:28.285 --> 00:03:31.540
it preserves the evidence ceiling of its source.

48
00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:37.431
At most, this visual explains the chapter's design rationale at argument

49
00:03:37.431 --> 00:03:42.242
support; it adds no empirical, deployment, safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI,

50
00:03:42.242 --> 00:03:47.533
or ASI result. The next chapter is Scalable Oversight and Adversarial

51
00:03:47.533 --> 00:03:48.495
AI Control.

52
00:03:48.835 --> 00:03:52.864
It takes responsibility for A system can ask a weaker human

53
00:03:52.864 --> 00:03:56.892
or model to judge a stronger system without recording whether the

54
00:03:56.892 --> 00:03:59.090
supervisor can see the relevant evidence.
